#~ nothing called `sideways` to look at
# `normal to <name>` where the name resolves to nothing.
#
# The camera has to point at something that exists. A name that does
# not resolve is a mistake — a misspelled plane, a face that was
# renamed — and defaulting to some other view would hide it: the
# picture would come out fine, of the wrong thing.
#
# Resolved in a phase after parsing, so a face of a solid can be named
# the same way a plane is once solids exist.

test draws normal to sideways "a square"
  wire(points: list(), segments: list())
